From 23b3a53bf3dc7fd095ab974a233571d55f02e2b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:22:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban-sync): an older feed copy of a run never reopens
 it; close dangling runs [daveey]

A run that ended within one sync round of an earlier write of the same row came back 'running' on the gateway and
on the Board (MacBook/hub/mini had 12/5/1 such rows). Child rows have no per-field clocks and push whole: the pull
applied the feed copy of an older state of the run (our own earlier op, whose outbox row the push had already
deleted, or the Board's lease-grant copy) over the newer local row, and the push then sent that clobbered row to
the Board. The card had moved on (current_run_id cleared), so no path reached the run again.

- apply: skip a feed copy of an existing child row while a local edit of it is pending in the outbox, and a
  task_runs copy at or below task_runs.sync_version (new local-only column: the Board version last applied or
  acknowledged; push records it from the op result)
- dispatcher: close_dangling_runs (in the orphan pass) closes runs still 'running' that are not their card's current
  run and are over 10 min old; on a synced board the close is pushed like any write

Tests: test_kanban_sync_run_rows.py (red before on the stale-lock reclaim, orphan sweep, run-ends-before-first-push,
newer-Board-write and sweep cases; a grant whose local CAS lost passes against a Board-faithful fake), the fake Board
gains opt-in lease runs. test_kanban_sync_apply ms test: clear the claim's pending outbox and give the later copy a
higher version (it relied on blind overwrite). Kanban t_01a17fd938a6621c.
